---
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "About" }]} />
  <h1>About the project</h1>
  <p class="page-intro">Who Owns Your DNA? is an advocacy and public-reference project built around an open, versioned policy dataset.</p>

  <section class="reading-width">
    <h2>Why this project exists</h2>
    <p>Genetic information can move through health care, research, consumer testing, insurance, employment, data markets, and law enforcement. The rules are fragmented across jurisdictions and legal frameworks. This project makes those sources easier to locate, compare, understand, and cite.</p>

    <h2>Intended audiences</h2>
    <p>The tracker is designed for researchers, journalists, advocates, policymakers, educators, and members of the public. It supports public understanding and source discovery. It does not replace legal research or advice.</p>

    <h2>Advocacy and factual summaries</h2>
    <p>Objective descriptions of legal text are separated from plain-language interpretation and advocacy context. Calls to action are labeled and visually distinct. Advocacy priorities do not change the status or wording of a legal record.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="resource-grid section-block">
    <section>
      <h2><a href={withBase("/methodology/")}>Methodology</a></h2>
      <p>Scope, inclusion criteria, source hierarchy, review, uncertainty, corrections, and versioning.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2><a href={withBase("/data/")}>Data</a></h2>
      <p>Structured records, machine-readable downloads, schema validation, and release planning.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2><a href={withBase("/cite/")}>Citation</a></h2>
      <p>Guidance for citing individual records, the website, and future dataset releases.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2><a href={withBase("/sources/nhgri/")}>NHGRI source archive</a></h2>
      <p>Source records retrieved from NHGRI, with the retrieval date, original wording, and provenance manifest preserved.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2><a href="https://www.ashg.org/advocacy/public-policy-positions/">ASHG policy positions</a></h2>
      <p>Explore professional-society perspectives on genetic privacy, data sharing, discrimination, genetic testing, research, and related policy questions.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section id="contribute" class="section-block reading-width">
    <h2>Contribute a source</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Locate the primary government source.</li>
      <li>Record the jurisdiction, identifier, legal status, and relevant dates.</li>
      <li>Propose factual wording and topic tags.</li>
      <li>Submit the source for human review.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Repository contribution instructions and a public contact method will be added before launch.</p>

    <h2>Contributors and acknowledgments</h2>
    <p>Contributor names and acknowledgments will be added with permission. This independent project is not affiliated with or endorsed by NIH, NLM, NCBI, ASHG, or another organization.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
